2025-11-21 01:42:19,796 - INFO - Function Requirement: Function Name: patient_risk_score
Description: Calculates a composite health risk score for a patient in the hospital system using the following formula:
- (patient.age / 100 * 30) +
- (patient.get_total_conditions() * 5 * 25/100) +
- (patient.get_average_severity() * 10 * 25/100) +
- (20 if any recent (last 90 days) records show abnormal vitals, else 0)

It retrieves the Patient object with hospital.get_patient(patient_id) and all recent records with hospital.get_recent_records(patient_id, 90), and uses Patient’s get_total_conditions() and get_average_severity(). For abnormal vitals, MedicalRecord.has_abnormal_vitals() is checked over recent records.

Parameters:
- hospital: Hospital — the Hospital object (from /home/aifahim/PycharmProjects/Self-Adapting-AI-Agent/dataset/patient_risk_analyzer/hospital.py)
- patient_id: str — patient’s unique identifier

Example:
patient_risk_score(hospital, "P123")

Composition:
- Uses Hospital.get_patient(patient_id)
- Uses Hospital.get_recent_records(patient_id, 90)
- Accesses Patient.get_total_conditions() and Patient.get_average_severity()
- Checks MedicalRecord.has_abnormal_vitals() for recent records

Returns: float — a value between 0.0 and 100.0 representing the patient’s risk score
